/T (2. Background / Motivation  Much of what students learn in school is shaped around exams and a fixed curriculum, leaving little room to explore how learning and inquiry work in the real world. Many students never get the chance to hear directly from young researchers about how curiosity and questions can grow into meaningful pursuits. A short, engaging talk session can open that door, helping students see learning as something alive and relevant rather than only exam material, while connecting them with a wider community of student researchers through NSSR. )
/E (2. Background / Motivation  Much of what students learn in school is shaped around exams and a fixed curriculum, leaving little room to explore how learning and inquiry work in the real world. Many students never get the chance to hear directly from young researchers about how curiosity and questions can grow into meaningful pursuits. A short, engaging talk session can open that door, helping students see learning as something alive and relevant rather than only exam material, while connecting them with a wider community of student researchers through NSSR. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
